===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|soile}}, {{m|enm|soyle}}, {{m|enm|sule|t=ground, earth}}, partly from {{der|en|xno|soyl|t=bottom, ground, pavement}}, from {{der|en|la|solium|t=seat, chair; throne}}, mistaken for {{der|en|la|solum|t=ground, foundation, earth, sole of the foot}}; and partly from {{inh|en|ang|sol|t=mud, mire, wet sand}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sulą|t=mud, spot}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sūl-|t=thick liquid}}. Cognate with {{cog|gml|söle|t=dirt, mud}}, {{cog|dum|sol|t=dirt, filth}}, {{cog|gmh|sol}}, {{m|gmh|söl|t=dirt, mud, mire}}, {{cog|da|søle|t=mud, muck}}. Compare {{cog|fr|seuil|t=level; threshold}} and {{m|fr|sol|t=soil, earth; ground}}. See also {{l|en|sole}}, {{l|en|soal}}, {{l|en|solum}}.

